{%- comment -%}
  CROOKSLDN: THE GETAWAY — first-visit discount popup.

  The offer is native theme HTML and paints instantly. The Base44 game is only
  fetched once someone presses RUN IT, which means the large majority who
  dismiss never pay for it at all — previously every visitor waited several
  seconds in front of a dimmed box for an iframe they were about to close.

  The app then starts on the game itself via ?screen=game, so the offer is not
  shown twice.

  Message contract with the app (window.postMessage):
    getaway:close                       shut the popup
    getaway:close  target: 'register'   they missed and chose the signup
    getaway:height { height: <px> }     app asking for a taller frame
    crooks-popup-close                  the previous app; still honoured

  The app must NOT send X-Frame-Options, or the browser refuses to render it
  here and the overlay is empty. That is a per-app toggle in the Base44 editor:
  Dashboard -> Security -> settings icon -> Security Headers -> "Prevent
  Embedding", which must stay OFF. Check with
  `curl -sI <url> | grep -i x-frame-options` before changing APP_URL.

  What the twenty-journey audit found, and where it went:

  1. FOCUS. It claimed role="dialog" aria-modal="true" and honoured none of it
     (15, 16). The shell now owns focus: it moves in, cycles, Escape closes,
     focus returns, and the rest of the page is aria-hidden throughout.
  2. THE ONE ATTEMPT. markSeen() fired on open, so a reflex close burned the
     only go (18). NOT NOW now suppresses for 14 days; a win suppresses for
     good; a bare close spends nothing.
  3. THE EMPTY BOX (13, 19). There is no box to be empty — the offer is theme
     HTML. The frame only appears after RUN IT, behind a holding line.
  4. THE COOKIE BANNER (02, 18, 20). Still waits for consent to be answered,
     and now also stays away while the menu drawer or cart drawer is open.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .ctc-overlay {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 2147483647;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 16px;
    background: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.9);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
    backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }
  .ctc-overlay[data-open] { opacity: 1 }

  .ctc-sheet {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 440px;
    height: 90vh;
    max-height: 680px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background: #0b0a0e;
    border: 1px solid rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.14);
    color: #f4f1ea;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    The offer, in theme HTML. Deliberately not a component and not styled from
    crooks.css: this has to paint in the same frame the overlay does, and a
    stylesheet that has not arrived yet would defeat the entire point.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  .ctc-offer {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 28px 24px;
    gap: 22px;
  }
  .ctc-title {
    font-family: 'VT323', 'CRX Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 42px;
    line-height: 0.95;
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .ctc-copy {
    font-family: 'CRX Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 300px;
    color: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.75);
  }
  .ctc-small {
    font-family: 'CRX Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 290px;
    color: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.45);
  }
  .ctc-actions { width: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px }
  .ctc-btn {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 0 16px;
    font-family: 'CRX Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #f4f1ea;
    background: #2b1b3d;
    border: 1px solid #4b276e;
    border-radius: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .ctc-btn:hover { border-color: #a77ac7 }
  .ctc-btn--quiet { background: transparent; border-color: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.22); color: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.7) }
  .ctc-btn--quiet:hover { color: #f4f1ea; border-color: #a77ac7 }
  .ctc-btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #a77ac7; outline-offset: 2px }

  .ctc-frame { width: 100%; flex: 1; border: 0; background: transparent; display: block }
  .ctc-holding {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: 'CRX Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.45);
  }

  .ctc-close {
    position: fixed;
    top: 12px;
    right: 14px;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 26px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: #f4f1ea;
    background: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.55);
    border: 1px solid rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.25);
    cursor: pointer;
    z-index: 2147483647;
  }
  .ctc-close:hover { background: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.12) }
  .ctc-close:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #a77ac7; outline-offset: 2px }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ctc-overlay { padding: 0 }
    .ctc-sheet { max-width: 100%; height: 100%; max-height: none; border: 0 }
    {%- comment -%}
      The app draws its own close control top-right inside the frame; on a phone
      that is the full width of the screen. Ours moves left so there are not two
      overlapping tap targets. It stays rather than being removed: it is the one
      way out the parent document controls, and the only one a screen reader can
      reach without entering a cross-origin frame.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    .ctc-close { right: auto; left: 10px }
    .ctc-title { font-size: 38px }
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    Landscape on a phone left roughly 300px of height for a 680px game, so the
    controls sat below the fold with nothing to scroll (journey 13).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media screen and (max-height: 500px) and (orientation: landscape) {
    .ctc-overlay { align-items: flex-start; overflow-y: auto; padding: 8px }
    .ctc-sheet { height: auto; min-height: 440px; max-height: none; max-width: 520px }
    .ctc-offer { padding: 18px 20px; gap: 14px }
    .ctc-title { font-size: 30px }
    .ctc-close { top: 6px; right: 8px; width: 36px; height: 36px; font-size: 20px }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .ctc-overlay { transition: none }
  }
</style>
<script>
  (function () {
    var APP_URL = 'https://crackthecuffs.base44.app';
    var APP_ORIGIN = 'https://crackthecuffs.base44.app';
    var SEEN = 'crooksldn_ctc_seen';      /* set on a win: never ask again */
    var SNOOZE = 'crooksldn_ctc_snooze';  /* NOT NOW: a timestamp, 14 days */
    var SNOOZE_DAYS = 14;
    var DELAY = 3000;
    var CONSENT = '#shopify-pc__banner, .shopify-pc__banner, #cookie-banner, .cookie-banner, [id*="cookie-consent"]';
    var CONSENT_WAIT_MS = 30000;
    var BUSY = '[data-crk-drawer][aria-hidden="false"], cart-drawer-component[open], dialog[open]';
    var opened = false;

    function qs(name) {
      try { return new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get(name); }
      catch (e) { return null; }
    }
    function isForced() { return qs('ctc') === '1'; }

    function get(k) { try { return window.localStorage.getItem(k); } catch (e) { return null; } }
    function set(k, v) { try { window.localStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch (e) {} }

    function hasWon() { return get(SEEN) === '1'; }
    function isSnoozed() {
      var t = parseInt(get(SNOOZE), 10);
      if (!t) return false;
      return (Date.now() - t) < SNOOZE_DAYS * 86400000;
    }

    function visible(sel) {
      try {
        var nodes = document.querySelectorAll(sel);
        for (var i = 0; i < nodes.length; i++) {
          if (nodes[i].offsetParent !== null || nodes[i].getClientRects().length) return true;
        }
      } catch (e) {}
      return false;
    }

    /* Never interrupt a shopper who is mid-task. The template gate in
       theme.liquid already keeps this to the homepage; this covers the states
       that are not a template — an open menu or cart drawer. */
    function busy() { return visible(BUSY); }

    function open() {
      if (opened) return;
      opened = true;

      var returnFocusTo = document.activeElement;

      var overlay = document.createElement('div');
      overlay.className = 'ctc-overlay';
      overlay.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
      overlay.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
      overlay.setAttribute('aria-label', 'CROOKSLDN: The Getaway');

      var closeBtn = document.createElement('button');
      closeBtn.className = 'ctc-close';
      closeBtn.type = 'button';
      closeBtn.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Close');
      closeBtn.innerHTML = '×';

      var sheet = document.createElement('div');
      sheet.className = 'ctc-sheet';

      /* ---- the offer, painted immediately ---- */
      var offer = document.createElement('div');
      offer.className = 'ctc-offer';

      var h = document.createElement('h2');
      h.className = 'ctc-title';
      h.textContent = 'CROOKSLDN: THE GETAWAY';

      var copy = document.createElement('p');
      copy.className = 'ctc-copy';
      copy.textContent = 'Crack the cuffs. 10% off your first order — code sent by text. Attempts unlimited.';

      var actions = document.createElement('div');
      actions.className = 'ctc-actions';

      var run = document.createElement('button');
      run.className = 'ctc-btn';
      run.type = 'button';
      run.textContent = 'RUN IT';

      var not = document.createElement('button');
      not.className = 'ctc-btn ctc-btn--quiet';
      not.type = 'button';
      not.textContent = 'NOT NOW';

      var small = document.createElement('p');
      small.className = 'ctc-small';
      /* No countdown, and no expiry mentioned before there is a code to expire.
         A ticking clock is on the brand's own rejected list, and naming a
         deadline for a prize the visitor has not won yet is the pressure
         selling the whole aesthetic is meant to avoid. */
      small.textContent = 'One code per player.';

      actions.appendChild(run);
      actions.appendChild(not);
      offer.appendChild(h);
      offer.appendChild(copy);
      offer.appendChild(actions);
      offer.appendChild(small);

      /* Close first in DOM order, so the first Tab reaches the way out rather
         than disappearing into a cross-origin frame. */
      overlay.appendChild(closeBtn);
      sheet.appendChild(offer);
      overlay.appendChild(sheet);

      var hidden = [];
      function hideBackground() {
        var kids = document.body.children;
        for (var i = 0; i < kids.length; i++) {
          var k = kids[i];
          if (k === overlay) continue;
          if (k.getAttribute('aria-hidden') === 'true') continue;
          k.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
          hidden.push(k);
        }
      }
      function showBackground() {
        for (var i = 0; i < hidden.length; i++) hidden[i].removeAttribute('aria-hidden');
        hidden = [];
      }

      var prevOverflow = document.documentElement.style.overflow;
      var frame = null;

      function close() {
        if (!overlay.parentNode) return;
        overlay.parentNode.removeChild(overlay);
        showBackground();
        document.documentElement.style.overflow = prevOverflow;
        document.removeEventListener('keydown', onKey, true);
        window.removeEventListener('message', onMsg);
        if (returnFocusTo && returnFocusTo.focus) {
          try { returnFocusTo.focus(); } catch (e) {}
        }
      }

      /* Tab cycles the controls that exist right now: the close button plus
         either the two offer buttons or the frame. */
      function stops() {
        var list = [closeBtn];
        if (frame) list.push(frame);
        else { list.push(run); list.push(not); }
        return list;
      }
      function onKey(e) {
        if (e.key === 'Escape') { close(); return; }
        if (e.key !== 'Tab') return;
        var list = stops();
        var i = list.indexOf(document.activeElement);
        e.preventDefault();
        var next = e.shiftKey ? list[(i <= 0 ? list.length : i) - 1] : list[(i + 1) % list.length];
        try { next.focus(); } catch (err) {}
      }

      function onMsg(e) {
        if (e.origin !== APP_ORIGIN) return;
        if (!e.data) return;
        var t = e.data.type;

        if (t === 'getaway:height') {
          var px = parseInt(e.data.height, 10);
          if (frame && px > 0) frame.style.height = px + 'px';
          return;
        }
        if (t !== 'getaway:close' && t !== 'crooks-popup-close') return;

        /* Choosing the signup after missing is real engagement, and it is the
           one hand-off the app asks us to complete. */
        if (e.data.target === 'register') {
          set(SEEN, '1');
          close();
          sendToRegister();
          return;
        }
        close();
      }

      /* The popup only renders on the homepage, so the intake section is always
         on this page — no anchor or navigation needed. Focus follows the scroll
         so a keyboard or screen-reader user lands on the field, not near it. */
      function sendToRegister() {
        var intake = document.querySelector('[data-crk-section="informant-intake"]');
        if (!intake) return;
        var reduce = false;
        try { reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches; } catch (e) {}
        try { intake.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }
        catch (err) { intake.scrollIntoView(); }
        var field = intake.querySelector('input[type="tel"], input[type="email"], input');
        if (!field || !field.focus) return;
        /* focus() WITHOUT preventScroll, deliberately. The smooth scroll above
           is presentation and can silently do nothing — it does in headless,
           and it does under some reduced-motion and older-browser conditions.
           If that happens and we suppress the focus scroll too, the shopper is
           left at the top of the page with focus on a field 2,500px below,
           which is worse than no hand-off at all. Letting focus scroll is the
           guarantee; the smooth scroll just makes it pleasant when it works. */
        window.setTimeout(function () {
          try { field.focus(); } catch (e2) {}
        }, reduce ? 0 : 400);
      }

      function runIt() {
        if (frame) return;
        var holding = document.createElement('div');
        holding.className = 'ctc-holding';
        holding.textContent = 'OPENING THE LOCK-UP…';
        sheet.replaceChild(holding, offer);

        frame = document.createElement('iframe');
        frame.className = 'ctc-frame';
        frame.title = 'Crack the Cuffs';
        frame.setAttribute('allow', 'clipboard-write');
        /* In the document from the start, or it never fetches — a detached
           iframe does not load, so swapping it in on its own load event is a
           wait that never ends. It is hidden behind the holding line instead. */
        frame.style.display = 'none';
        sheet.appendChild(frame);
        frame.addEventListener('load', function () {
          frame.style.display = 'block';
          if (holding.parentNode) holding.parentNode.removeChild(holding);
          try { frame.focus(); } catch (e) {}
        });
        frame.src = APP_URL + '?screen=game';
      }

      run.addEventListener('click', runIt);
      /* Fetch the app the moment intent shows, so the tap has a head start. */
      run.addEventListener('mouseenter', prefetch);
      run.addEventListener('touchstart', prefetch, { passive: true });

      not.addEventListener('click', function () {
        set(SNOOZE, String(Date.now()));
        close();
      });
      closeBtn.addEventListener('click', close);
      overlay.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target === overlay) close(); });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', onKey, true);
      window.addEventListener('message', onMsg);

      document.body.appendChild(overlay);
      hideBackground();
      document.documentElement.style.overflow = 'hidden';
      requestAnimationFrame(function () { overlay.setAttribute('data-open', ''); });
      try { closeBtn.focus(); } catch (e) {}
    }

    var prefetched = false;
    function prefetch() {
      if (prefetched) return;
      prefetched = true;
      var l = document.createElement('link');
      l.rel = 'prefetch';
      l.href = APP_URL + '?screen=game';
      document.head.appendChild(l);
    }

    function preconnect() {
      var l = document.createElement('link');
      l.rel = 'preconnect';
      l.href = APP_ORIGIN;
      l.crossOrigin = '';
      document.head.appendChild(l);
    }

    function whenClear(done) {
      if (!visible(CONSENT) && !busy()) { done(); return; }
      var giveUpAt = Date.now() + CONSENT_WAIT_MS;
      var poll = window.setInterval(function () {
        if ((!visible(CONSENT) && !busy()) || Date.now() > giveUpAt) {
          window.clearInterval(poll);
          done();
        }
      }, 400);
    }

    function schedule() {
      if (isForced()) { preconnect(); open(); return; }
      if (hasWon() || isSnoozed()) return;
      preconnect();
      window.setTimeout(function () { whenClear(open); }, DELAY);
    }

    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', schedule);
    } else {
      schedule();
    }
  })();
</script>
